<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LIVETAP app-target privacy manifest.

  WHY THE APP TARGET NEEDS ONE EVEN THOUGH CAPACITOR SHIPS ONE
  `node_modules/@capacitor/ios/Capacitor/Capacitor/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy` exists (verified
  2026-09-11) but declares an EMPTY `NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes` array, and `@capacitor/preferences`
  ships no manifest at all while calling `UserDefaults.standard` directly
  (node_modules/@capacitor/preferences/ios/Sources/PreferencesPlugin/Preferences.swift:19).
  Required-reason API usage that a dependency does not declare becomes the app target's
  responsibility, so `NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeUserDefaults` is declared here.

  BEFORE FIRST SUBMISSION — two things must be checked by a human:
  1. The reason code string below. `CA92.1` is the commonly used code for "access user defaults
     only for this app or its app group". It could NOT be verified against Apple's own
     required-reason API page from the build host: that page is rendered client-side and returns
     only its title to a plain fetch. Status: UNVERIFIED. Read the reason tables in Xcode's
     privacy-manifest editor (or the live Apple page in a browser) and correct the string if it
     differs — a mismatched reason is a rejection, not a warning.
  2. `NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes` below. It is empty because the LIVETAP MVP binary collects
     nothing: no analytics SDK, no crash reporter, no LIVETAP account, no LIVETAP server that
     receives media. Camera and microphone data is encoded on device and pushed directly to the
     third-party channels the user connected, which is the user's own transmission, not developer
     collection. The App Store Connect "App Privacy Details" questionnaire is a SEPARATE surface
     with a broader reading of "collect", and the moment crash reporting, analytics or any
     LIVETAP-operated service is added, both this file and that questionnaire must change in the
     same release. See docs/release/APP_STORE_READINESS.md items A17/A19.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- LIVETAP does not track. No IDFA, no ad SDK, no data broker, no cross-app linking. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>

	<!-- No domains are used for tracking, so this array stays empty (required when tracking is false). -->
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<!--
	  Empty for the MVP. See note 2 above before changing.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!--
			  Reached through @capacitor/preferences, which stores non-secret local settings
			  (chosen content intent, quality preset, Moment layout) in UserDefaults.standard.
			  Secrets never go here: OAuth tokens and stream keys belong in the Keychain.
			-->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<!-- UNVERIFIED exact string — see note 1 above. -->
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
